  "published": "2026-07-31T00:07:49.97Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Donor imports are now streamed: peak memory is the largest single tensor rather than the whole donor, so a 20 GB donor imports in a few GB of RAM instead of ~75 GB. This covers `transfer`, distillation teachers (`loadTeacher`) and `merge-models`, across .gguf files, single .safetensors files and sharded directories (model.safetensors.index.json); shards holding nothing the mapping wants are never opened. MERGE: model merging holds one tensor per input model instead of one whole model per input — merging three 20 GB models no longer needs 60 GB before the first parameter is merged. GGUF: five new encodings decode — Q5_0 (previously skipped silently, which cost 133 of 219 tensors on a typical Q4_K_M donor and left most weights randomly initialized), plus BF16, Q4_1, Q5_1 and Q8_1; thirteen ggml types are now supported. The embedded tokenizer can be extracted from a .gguf (vocab.json + merges.txt), so a downloaded donor no longer needs its tokenizer fetched separately. CORRECTNESS: attention head counts are read from the donor instead of inferred from tensor shapes — shape inference is ambiguous and picks the coarsest split, so a 14-head/2-KV model was silently built as 7/1 with dimensions that still matched. GGUF states them in metadata; safetensors donors read them from the sibling config.json. A transfer that finds fewer than half the weights the mapping asks for is now refused rather than producing a model that looks trained but is mostly random. SERVING: OpenAI-compatible fixes for agentic clients (Crush, and anything on charmbracelet/fantasy) — usage reported in a trailing stream chunk when stream_options.include_usage is set, tool results attributed to the call that produced them via tool_call_id, array-form message content accepted, and prompts exceeding the model context refused with 400 context_length_exceeded instead of failing inside the generation core. `fuuga-serve --chat-template` selects the donor prompt format (fuuga|llama3|phi3|phi4|gemma3|gemma4|chatml|qwen|mistral, or a raw template) — serving donor weights behind Fuuga role markers degrades output and suppresses tool calling. CONSTRAINED DECODING: several defects fixed — `required` was parsed but never enforced (so \"{}\" satisfied any object schema), object keys were unconstrained, enum values were not restricted to their allowed strings, and nested values never required their opening delimiter, which made every nested-object or nested-string json_schema request emit malformed JSON. TRAINING DATA: 30 built-in tool-calling SFT examples in the byte-exact format the generation parser accepts.",
